cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LocusAtlas in your work, please cite it as below. Formerly named EpiLog: versions up to v1.2.0 were archived under the old name; the concept DOI is the same for every version."
title: "LocusAtlas: A Curated Genomic Safe Harbor Catalog and Post-Edit Silencing Registry"
abstract: >-
  LocusAtlas (formerly EpiLog) is a literature-derived catalog of genomic safe harbor loci and their
  post-editing expression/silencing outcomes, with per-record confidence
  tiers, stability/duration summaries, tissue context, and genome-build
  annotations, spanning human, mouse, dog, pig, goat, cattle, zebrafish, and
  Drosophila melanogaster. It also provides a private, per-account registry
  for logging new gene-editing experiments and tracking silencing status over
  time.
